  "diagnosis": {
    "classification": "evidence_supported_sequential_update_recency_interference",
    "confidence": "supported_hypothesis_not_causal_proof",
    "finding": "The scene-only joint warmup proved that the adapter could simultaneously satisfy all six deduplicated target sides, but the main stage applied a separate optimizer update after each single counterfactual unit. The gate later reached five of six complete units at epoch 11 and regressed to four of six at epoch 12 even while train loss and aggregate gate hinge improved. This pattern is consistent with later single-unit updates partially overwriting earlier unit-specific behavior.",
    "evidence": [
      "Warmup step 28 passed 6/6 sides with minimum margin 0.105218805372715 above the configured 0.1 target and mean margin 0.14505083858966827.",
      "The main stage used gradient accumulation 1, one counterfactual pair unit per microbatch, and therefore one optimizer update per unit for six ordered updates per epoch.",
      "The gate peaked at 5/6 complete changed units in epoch 11, then fell to 4/6 in epoch 12.",
      "From epoch 11 to epoch 12, train loss decreased from 12.84913412729899 to 11.913546085357666 and gate hinge decreased from 0.1666666716337204 to 0.1223958358168602 while complete changed-unit correctness regressed, so the aggregate scalar objectives did not preserve the all-unit gate state."
    ],
    "not_proven": "The artifacts do not retain per-update gate evaluations, so they do not prove which particular update caused the regression. The diagnosis is the mechanism best supported by the measured trajectory and exact single-unit optimizer schedule."
  },
